<title>CANADA: Canada Q4 current account deficit C$1.703 bln.</title>
<headline>Canada Q4 current account deficit C$1.703 bln.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada had a current account deficit of C$1.703 billion, seasonally adjusted, in the fourth quarter of 1996 after a C$288 million surplus in the previous quarter, Statistics Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>	(Blns C$, S/A)   Q4 96	  Q3 96	   Q4 95</p>
<p>Current account	  -1.70	  +0.55	   -0.33</p>
<p>Merchandise		+6.69	  +9.71	   +8.46</p>
<p>Total non-merchandise  -8.39	  -9.42	   -8.79</p>
<p>   Services		-1.94	  -2.53	   -2.26</p>
<p>   Investment income   -6.72	  -7.13	   -6.59</p>
<p>   Transfers (millions)+0.26	  +0.24	   +0.07</p>
<p>			     Q4 96	  Q3 96	   Q4 95</p>
<p>Total receipts	   82.74	  84.33	   80.21</p>
<p>Total payments	   84.44	  84.05	   80.54</p>
<p>For the whole year 1996, Canada's current account deficit fell sharply to C$1.69 billion from C$11.20 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billions of Canadian dollars on a seasonally adjusted basis.</p>
<p>Economists surveyed by Reuters had forecast a current account deficit of C$3.0 billion in the quarter.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
